;; Regulatory source register for JPN-DIGITAL — the Digital Agency
;; (デジタル庁), its gBizID identity track and its digital-government
;; procurement/statutory basis.
;;
;; README.md says facts.cljc is "the ONLY source of regulatory-requirement
;; facts the actor may cite" — but until this file existed, nothing mapped a
;; claim in that file to a live authority. This is that list.
;;
;; Shape is tx-data (a vector of entity maps), like every other EDN corpus in
;; this workspace, so it loads with
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "facts.edn")))
;; :source/id is the join key. A law or page not in this table has NO
;; spec-basis for this repository — extend the table, never invent an id or a
;; URL.
;;
;; VERIFIED BY `nbb scripts/verify-facts.cljk`, which re-fetches every entry.
;; Each carries a :source/verify tag naming WHICH check establishes it:
;;
;;   :e-gov-law-id   Resolve the law id through the e-Gov law API and require
;;                   the title and the law number to still match. HTTP status
;;                   is never consulted here and must not be:
;;                   laws.e-gov.go.jp is a single-page app that answers
;;                   HTTP 200 for /law/<anything>, renders "not found"
;;                   client-side, and therefore cannot tell a real citation
;;                   from an invented one.
;;
;;   :page-identity  Fetch and require four things together: a 2xx, a final
;;                   URL that is still the page asked for, the declared
;;                   charset, and the <title> recorded below.
;;
;;   :page-text      All of :page-identity, plus every string in
;;                   :page/must-contain present in the de-tagged body.
;;
;; THE HOST ASSUMPTIONS ARE MEASURED AT RUN TIME, NOT DATED IN A COMMENT.
;; The :host-behaviour entities below say what each host does with a path that
;; does not exist. The verifier fetches a nonexistent path on every host in the
;; register and fails if the answer has changed. A dated note saying "measured
;; to refuse correctly" degrades into a constant the moment it is written; a
;; declaration the run re-measures cannot.
;;
;; MEASURED 2026-08-30, THE DAY THIS REGISTER WAS WRITTEN, AND DIFFERENT PER
;; HOST — WHICH IS WHY THEY ARE PER-HOST ENTITIES AND NOT A SHARED DEFAULT:
;;
;;   www.digital.go.jp   answers 404 for a path that does not exist, with a
;;                       real ページ ("404｜デジタル庁", 2828 bytes) AT the
;;                       requested URL. 404 is not 2xx, so status still
;;                       discriminates. Content-Type carries no charset; the
;;                       encoding is declared only by a <meta> tag — the
;;                       verifier reads the meta tag when the header is silent.
;;
;;   gbiz-id.go.jp       answers 404 with a generic "エラー" page (4071 bytes),
;;                       declared charset=UTF-8 in the header. The title differs
;;                       from every real page on the host, which is what makes
;;                       :page-identity mean something here on top of status.
;;
;;   pr.gbiz-id.go.jp    answers 403 with a 111-byte application/xml body and
;;                       NO <title> at all — an S3-style XML error document, not
;;                       an HTML page. A checker written to read <title> off
;;                       every refusal would see nil here and might misreport a
;;                       host that answered perfectly clearly. Status still
;;                       discriminates: 403 is not 2xx.
;;
;; None of the three hosts challenged this client while the register was built
;; (seven serial probes, seconds apart). None of them is declared
;; challenge-prone; if one starts, the verifier refuses on it and says so
;; rather than reporting a pass it did not earn.
;;
;; :source/covers says why an entry is in a Digital-Agency procurement and
;; identity register. Claims stop at the level actually checked — law identity,
;; and for the pages the title, the URL, the charset and the strings read on
;; 2026-08-30. No article text and no PDF is asserted, because none was read.

[
 ;; ── What each host does with a path that does not exist ────────────────────
 ;; Re-measured on every run. A change here invalidates the check that rests
 ;; on it, which is the point of writing it down as data.

 {:source/id "host.www-digital-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "www.digital.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "デジタル庁 itself. Answers 404 with a 2828-byte
                404｜デジタル庁 page served at the requested URL, charset
                declared only in the <meta> tag, not the header. The page is
                REAL — that is a genuine soft 404, and any 2xx here would be
                the failure signal."}

 {:source/id "host.gbiz-id-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "gbiz-id.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 404
  :source/note "The GビズID service host. Answers 404 with a 4071-byte
                エラー page at the requested URL. Its title is generic —
                エラー, no site name — so it is the TITLE of the real pages,
                not of this one, that carries the discrimination."}

 {:source/id "host.pr-gbiz-id-go-jp"
  :source/kind :host-behaviour
  :host/name "pr.gbiz-id.go.jp"
  :host/missing-path :refuses
  :host/missing-status 403
  :source/note "The GビズID overview site. Answers 403 with a 111-byte
                application/xml document and no <title> — an object-store
                error page, not HTML. Refuses a DIFFERENT status (403) than
                the other two hosts (404) for the same kind of mistake, which
                is exactly why this is declared per host and not assumed."}

